    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Identity Information — Employee Names", "technique": "T1589.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-12 09:02:11 CEST, Suricata logged a burst of 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' alerts with data.srcip=91.211.247.155 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177 (corporate web application). The crawl walked a fixed list of staff/leadership directory paths — data.url values including /team, /our-team, /leadership, /executives, /people, /staff, /directory, /about/team, /meet-the-team, /company/people — at a deliberate ~16-second inter-request cadence. The pacing is slow enough to evade naive 'X requests per second' web-flood thresholds, fast enough to enumerate ~24 staff page paths in ~5 minutes. The fixed-path-list pattern (not random spidering) is the signature of name-harvesting tooling that targets predictable HR/about-us page structures to extract real employee Firstname Lastname strings.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signature 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' triggered with data.srcip=91.211.247.155 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177, sequential data.url values matching a known staff-directory wordlist, all sharing rotating but consistent data.http.user_agent values. rule.mitre.id was tagged T1589.003 (Gather Victim Identity Information: Employee Names) by the correlation rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Identity Information — Search API Name Enumeration", "technique": "T1589.003", "what_happened": "At 09:08:40 CEST (~1-minute pause after the staff-page crawl ended ~09:07), the same data.srcip=91.211.247.155 began hitting search endpoints — data.url values /search?q=, /api/users/search?q=, /directory/search?query= — with sequential two-character name prefixes (jo, al, bo, mi, da, la, sa, ch, st, pa, ma, an, fr, er, li, ju, ro, pi, vi). Each short prefix is designed to make a corporate search endpoint return ALL employee cards whose name begins with those letters, harvesting the full employee roster from a feature that is normally benign. Suricata fired a custom 'search API enumeration pattern' rule on the sequential single-source query bursts at ~18-second cadence.", "chain_reason": "Same data.srcip=91.211.247.155 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177 with data.url containing /search and /api/users/search and /directory/search, query strings cycling through short 2-char alphabetic prefixes — the canonical search-endpoint roster-enumeration pattern. rule.description 'Web search endpoint enumeration - sequential name queries from single source'.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:08:40+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Gather Victim Identity Information — Directory & vCard Probes", "technique": "T1591.004", "what_happened": "At 09:15:30 CEST (~45-second pause after Phase 2), the same data.srcip=91.211.247.155 probed directory-export and contact-protocol endpoints — data.url values /.well-known/carddav, /contacts/export, /people.vcf, /employees.json, /staff.json, /team.json, /api/v1/directory, /api/v1/contacts, /owa/directory, /autodiscover/autodiscover.xml — looking for a bulk export of the employee directory in vCard or JSON form. This is the highest-value harvesting step: a single successful /employees.json or carddav response yields the entire org chart with names, titles, and often email addresses. Suricata fired 'ET SCAN Aggressive Web Crawl' and directory-probe signatures across the 09:15-09:21 window.", "chain_reason": "Same data.srcip=91.211.247.155 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177, data.url values matching directory-export wordlist (.well-known/carddav, employees.json, staff.json, api/v1/directory, owa/directory, autodiscover.xml), ~22-second cadence. The progression staff-pages → search-API → directory-export is the methodical name-harvesting workflow; rule.mitre.id tagged T1591.004 (Gather Victim Org Information: Identify Roles).", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:15:30+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Reconnaissance / Cumulative Volume", "technique": "T1589.003", "what_happened": "Across the 09:02-09:23 window (~21 minutes), Suricata + Wazuh aggregated ~38 distinct alerts with data.srcip=91.211.247.155 against data.dstip=10.108.57.177 — combining aggressive-web-crawl alerts (Phase 1), search-API enumeration alerts (Phase 2), and directory-probe alerts (Phase 3). Wazuh rule 31101 (high-volume web requests from a single source IP) also fired on the cumulative request count. The single-external-src + fixed-wordlist + polite-cadence + three-phase progression is the canonical employee-name-harvesting fingerprint that MITRE T1589.003 describes. The harvested names feed directly into T1589.002 (email format enumeration) and T1598 (spearphishing) as the next stages of the kill chain.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation rule 'High-volume web reconnaissance from single external source' (rule.groups containing 'suricata' + 'web' + 'recon') fired on aggregate count of web-recon alerts from the same data.srcip within a 30-minute window. The MITRE mapping T1589.003 (Gather Victim Identity Information: Employee Names) was attached automatically by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:21:00+0200"}
